[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged as one issue and is now closed. Read report by report, it
was more than one issue. Engineering fixed the parser and retired the booking-v3 form. Neither
change touches the reports where a date moved by one day, and nobody owns those yet.

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 is closed, but not every problem in it is. Before you tell a tenant their date bug is
fixed, check which problem their report belongs to.
</Callout>

## The problems

<ProblemTable
  ticket={4471}
  issues={{
    parser: 'https://github.com/kevinw9092/s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1',
    hint: 'https://github.com/kevinw9092/s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2',
    shift: 'https://github.com/kevinw9092/s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/3',
  }}
/>

## How to tell them apart

- **`parser`**: the tenant writes dates day first (every tenant on file does, `en-GB` and
  `en-IE` included) and the report came in by app, by email, or through a booking-v2 form. The
  shared parser read the date month first, so day and month swapped: 4 July became 7 April.
  Fixed: the parser now reads day-first dates for these locales.
- **`hint`**: the report came through the booking form on a **booking-v3** tenant. That form
  printed `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People typed what it showed, month first; the form
  read the date the tenant's way, day first. It looked like the parser bug, so it got merged
  with it, but the parser fix does not cover it. Won't fix: the booking-v3 form is retired, so
  no new bookings come through it. Bookings already made through it keep their swapped dates.
- **`shift`**: the date is one day off, not swapped. An invite one day early, every June booking
  a day off, an invite that arrived before the booking was made, a guest in Lisbon and a guest
  in Toronto shown different days for one meeting. Day/month order cannot do that; a time zone
  or offset can. The desk noted these reports as a one-day move, then filed them under the
  tenant's cause, so the parser fix closed them with #4471. They are still open.

Ignore the intake tag when you sort these. It is guessed from the reporter's browser locale, not
from the tenant, and it disagrees with the tenant on many reports in this ticket.

## Why one ticket

Reports were merged on matching subject lines ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)).
Subjects like "Date is wrong" fit all three bugs, so all three ended up here. The table the
incident page shows already splits out `hint`, but labels it "no ticket of its own":

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## What to do

1. A new `shift` report (one day off, not swapped) is not #4471. File it under the `shift`
   ticket linked above, which stays open until someone owns the time-zone handling.
2. A new day/month swap from a day-first tenant after the parser fix is a regression: open a new
   ticket, do not reopen #4471.
3. Tenants that booked through booking-v3 may still hold swapped dates. Tell them to check
   bookings made before the form was retired.
4. Replace decision 0001 with a new record: match on cause (tenant, channel, form), not subject.

